Play it with Asciiverse
=======================

With av, the Asciiverse client (https://asciiverse.sh):

    av install solitty
    av play solitty

The original README follows.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -*-org-*-

* solitty
  Ncurses-based klondike solitaire game.

  #+CAPTION: solitty gameplay
  [[./resources/solitty.gif]]

** Dependencies
   - Terminal emulator with UTF-8 support
   - C library with multibyte locales support
   - Ncurses with wide-char/UTF-8 support

** Install
*** From source
**** Install Ncurses
     solitty depends on Ncurses. Some platforms provide it out of the box
     and some don't, so you might need to install it yourself.

***** Ubuntu
      #+begin_src bash
      sudo apt-get install libncurses5-dev libncursesw5-dev
      #+end_src

***** macOS
      macOS has Ncurses with wide character support out of the box, so *there's
      nothing you need to do*.

**** Build and install solitty
     #+begin_src bash
     git clone https://github.com/theasciiverse/solitty.git
     cd solitty
     make
     sudo make install
     #+end_src

** Play
   Run in your favorite shell:

   #+begin_src bash
   solitty
   #+end_src

** Usage
   #+begin_src text
   usage: ./solitty [OPTIONS]
     -v, --version              Show version
     -h, --help                 Show this message
     -p, --passes               Number of passes through the deck  (default: 3)
         --four-color-deck      Draw unique card suit colors       (default: false)
         --no-background-color  Don't draw background color        (default: false)
   #+end_src

** Development
*** Get the code
    #+begin_src bash
    git clone https://github.com/theasciiverse/solitty.git
    #+end_src

*** Run the unit tests
    #+begin_src bash
    make test
    #+end_src

*** [[https://invisible-island.net/ncurses/man/ncurses.3x.html][Ncurses documentation]]

*** [[https://tldp.org/HOWTO/NCURSES-Programming-HOWTO/][Ncurses programming HOWTO]]

